{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only data variable scored by a sampling statement is the top-level observation `y`, which is observed exactly once with `y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma)` after all parameters have received built-in priors. Other data variables (`N`, `n_treatment`, `n_airport`, `treatment`, and `airport`) are context inputs used as sizes and indices, not protected observations.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> n_treatment;
  int<lower=0> n_airport;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=n_treatment> treatment;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=n_airport> airport;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma;
  real<lower=0> sigma_gamma;
  real<lower=0> sigma_delta;
  vector[n_treatment] gamma;
  vector[n_airport] delta;
  real mu;
}
model {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  sigma ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_gamma ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_delta ~ uniform(0, 100);

  mu ~ normal(0, 100);

  gamma ~ normal(0, sigma_gamma);
  delta ~ normal(0, sigma_delta);

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = mu + gamma[treatment[i]] + delta[airport[i]];
  }

  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":4,"airport":[2,3,2,3],"n_airport":3,"n_treatment":3,"treatment":[1,3,1,3],"y":[2.0,3.0,2.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
